{
    "background_story": "Julian was born into a family where tradition and patriarchal values were deeply ingrained. His father, a stern but fair man, was the undisputed head of the household. Julian's upbringing was marked by a strong emphasis on discipline, hard work, and respect for authority. As the eldest son, he was expected to follow in his father's footsteps and take over the family business. Julian struggled with the weight of these expectations, feeling stifled by the rigid gender roles and the pressure to conform. Despite this, he remained devoted to his family and worked tirelessly to prove himself worthy of his father's legacy. As he grew older, Julian began to forge his own path, blending tradition with modern values and becoming a leader in his own right. His journey was a testament to the complexities of patricentric cultures and the importance of finding one's own identity within them.",
